<p>Printing starts from the last page.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>If the application you are using has a similar 
 function, do not make settings with the application's function.</p></li>
<li><p>If you use this function when applying 2 sided 
 printing to a document with an odd number of pages, the blank last page 
 will also be included in the print count.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Output Settings</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Reverse Order 
 Printing</span> check box.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
